-- Skrypt tłumaczący istniejące działy pomocy
UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Transport', `content_en` = '<h2>Transport &mdash; how oil reaches the market</h2>\n<p>Extracted oil <strong>does not sell itself</strong>. You must have transport to sell it. No transport = 0 revenue.</p>\n<h3>Types of transport</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>🛢️ Pipeline</strong> &mdash; the best option. Low maintenance cost, high capacity, but requires purchase and maintenance.</li>\n<li><strong>🚛 Trucks</strong> &mdash; more expensive to operate, but easy to start. Good for the beginning or as a backup.</li>\n<li><strong>🚢 Tanker</strong> &mdash; for large producers. Highest capacity, but high costs.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Capacity</h3>\n<p>Every transport has a limit &mdash; how many barrels of oil it can transport to the market in one tick. If your well produces more than the capacity, the surplus <strong>goes to storage</strong> (if there is space) or is lost.</p>\n<h3>Transport (losses)</h3>\n<p>Pipelines lose some oil in transport (leakage, evaporation). Typically 2&ndash;8%. The worse the technical condition of the pipeline, the higher the losses. Track losses in the <strong>Technical</strong> tab.</p>\n<h3>Transport breakdowns</h3>\n<p>Pipelines can fail &mdash; leak or mechanical damage. During a breakdown, transport is suspended or severely limited. Repair the pipeline as soon as possible &mdash; every tick without a sale is a loss of revenue.</p>' WHERE `slug` = 'transport';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Storage', `content_en` = '<h2>Storage &mdash; a buffer for oil</h2>\n<p>Storage holds oil that could not be sold immediately &mdash; e.g. when transport is busy or capacity is too small.</p>\n<h3>How does it work?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Each player has one storage with a specific capacity (default 10,000 barrels).</li>\n<li>When transport is full, surplus production goes to storage.</li>\n<li>When storage is full &mdash; the surplus is <strong>lost forever</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>When does the storage fill up?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Transport breakdown &mdash; production has no way to reach the market.</li>\n<li>Pipeline capacity too small relative to production.</li>\n<li>High production with small storage.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>⚠️ <strong>Note:</strong> A full storage is an alarm signal &mdash; you must either increase transport or reduce production. Oil in an overflowing storage is lost!</p>\n<h3>Storage expansion</h3>\n<p>You can expand storage in the <strong>Technical &rarr; Expand storage</strong> tab. It costs a one-time fee, but increases capacity.</p>' WHERE `slug` = 'magazyn';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Breakdowns and incidents', `content_en` = '<h2>Breakdowns and incidents &mdash; something always breaks</h2>\n<p>In the oil industry, breakdowns are inevitable. Your company must be prepared for them &mdash; financially and operationally.</p>\n<h3>Types of incidents</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Micro-breakdown</strong> &mdash; minor fault, -5&ndash;10% production. Repaired automatically in the next tick.</li>\n<li><strong>Minor breakdown</strong> &mdash; -20% production, repaired automatically, but costs money.</li>\n<li><strong>Medium breakdown</strong> &mdash; -50% production. Requires manual repair in the Technical tab.</li>\n<li><strong>Disaster (blowout/explosion)</strong> &mdash; production stopped. Well damaged. Very expensive repair. Can lead to bankruptcy if you have no reserves.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>What increases the risk of breakdown?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Low technical condition of the well (below 40% &mdash; alarm!).</li>\n<li>High wear_level &mdash; the higher it is, the more frequent and severe the breakdowns.</li>\n<li>No technician or HSE.</li>\n<li>High political risk in the region.</li>\n<li>Intensive exploitation for a long time.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>How to minimize the risk?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Maintain technical condition above 60%. Order repairs regularly.</li>\n<li>Always have a technician and HSE assigned to the well.</li>\n<li>Watch the wear_level &mdash; when it exceeds 70%, consider temporarily shutting down the well.</li>\n<li>Keep a cash reserve for repairs (min. 20&ndash;30% of monthly costs).</li>\n</ul>' WHERE `slug` = 'awarie';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Bank and loans', `content_en` = '<h2>Bank &mdash; financing development</h2>\n<p>Short on cash to buy a well or repair after a disaster? The bank offers loans &mdash; but remember they have to be repaid. One note: the bank takes many factors into account.</p>\n<h3>How to get a loan?</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to the <strong>Bank</strong> tab.</li>\n<li>Choose the amount and repayment period.</li>\n<li>Accept the interest rate.</li>\n<li>Funds arrive in your account immediately.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Repayment</h3>\n<p>Installments are deducted automatically every tick or every day (depending on the agreement). If you do not have funds for the installment &mdash; penalty interest is charged and the risk of a bailiff entering increases.</p>\n<h3>Loan collateral</h3>\n<p>The bank may require collateral &mdash; e.g. a well or storage. If you do not repay the loan, the secured assets may be seized.</p>\n<h3>When to take a loan?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ To buy a profitable well &mdash; if ROI (return on investment) is shorter than 5 days.</li>\n<li>✅ For an emergency repair after a disaster &mdash; so as not to lose the entire infrastructure.</li>\n<li>❌ Do not take a loan when the oil price is very low &mdash; you can fall into a spiral of debt.</li>\n<li>❌ Do not take more than you can repay from 3-day production.</li>\n</ul>' WHERE `slug` = 'bank';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Bankruptcy and restructuring', `content_en` = '<h2>Bankruptcy &mdash; what does it mean and how to get out?</h2>\n<p>Bankruptcy is a serious situation, but not the end of the game. You can get out of it &mdash; if you act quickly and smartly.</p>\n<h3>How does bankruptcy happen?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Your company has a negative balance for too long.</li>\n<li>You do not pay loan installments and penalties accrue.</li>\n<li>A bailiff seizes assets and you lack funds for current costs.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Stages of financial problems</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>🟡 Financial risk</strong> &mdash; balance is dropping, but you are not bankrupt yet. Time to act!</li>\n<li><strong>🟠 Bailiff</strong> &mdash; the company is under execution. Part of the assets may be seized.</li>\n<li><strong>🔴 Bankruptcy / Restructuring</strong> &mdash; blockade of new investments and loans. Rescue mode.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Restructuring mode</h3>\n<p>When you enter bankruptcy, the <strong>Rescue Panel</strong> will appear. In this mode:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You cannot take new loans or buy wells.</li>\n<li>You can sell assets to pay off debts.</li>\n<li>Turn off expensive wells &mdash; leave only those that bring profit.</li>\n<li>After paying off obligations and reaching a positive balance &mdash; status returns to normal.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>How to avoid bankruptcy?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Always keep a cash reserve (min. 3-day operational costs).</li>\n<li>Monitor the ratio of revenue to OPEX &mdash; if costs are higher than profits, change something.</li>\n<li>Do not develop too fast &mdash; better 2 profitable wells than 6 in debt.</li>\n<li>Before taking a loan, check if the installment fits within your monthly profit.</li>\n</ul>' WHERE `slug` = 'bankructwo';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Well statuses', `content_en` = '<h2>Well statuses — what does each color mean?</h2>\n<p>Every well has a status visible on the main board. The status determines whether the well produces oil and whether operating costs are charged.</p>\n\n<h3>Production statuses</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>🟢 Active</strong> — the well produces oil approximately every 5 minutes. Requires an assigned operator and functional transport.</li>\n<li><strong>⏸ Suspended — no crew</strong> — the well is not producing due to the lack of an operator or technician. Operating costs are still charged. Hire an employee in the HR tab.</li>\n<li><strong>💸 Suspended — no cash</strong> — the company has no funds to cover operating costs. The well stopped automatically. Pay off your debts or sell unnecessary assets.</li>\n<li><strong>🏭 Suspended — storage full</strong> — production goes to storage, but it is full. Excess oil is lost irretrievably. Increase transport capacity or expand storage.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Emergency statuses</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>👷 No operator</strong> — no operator is assigned to the well. Go to the Technical tab and assign an employee.</li>\n<li><strong>🔧 No technician</strong> — lack of a technician causes accelerated equipment wear. Technical condition drops twice as fast as normal.</li>\n<li><strong>🔴 Breakdown</strong> — serious technical fault. Production suspended. Manual repair required in the Technical tab.</li>\n<li><strong>🚨 Blowout</strong> — industrial disaster. The well is destroyed. Repair is very expensive — consider selling the well.</li>\n<li><strong>☣️ Contamination</strong> — leakage of hazardous substances. Production suspended until the area is cleaned up.</li>\n<li><strong>⛔ Seized by bailiff</strong> — the well was taken over in the course of bailiff execution. Pay off your debt to recover it.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>What affects production volume?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Technical condition</strong> — decreases over time. Below 40%, the risk of breakdown increases significantly. Order regular repairs.</li>\n<li><strong>Operator</strong> — operator rating (1–10) directly multiplies well efficiency.</li>\n<li><strong>Equipment tier</strong> — higher equipment level (Basic / Standard / Advanced / Premium) increases baseline production.</li>\n<li><strong>Geological layer</strong> — the deeper it is (Shallow → Ultra deep), the more oil, but also higher risks and costs.</li>\n<li><strong>Transport</strong> — transport capacity limits how much oil goes on sale. Excess goes to storage or is lost.</li>\n</ul>' WHERE `slug` = 'statusy';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Tips for beginners', `content_en` = '<h2>OilCorp Golden Rules</h2>\n\n<h3>🟢 Do this</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Always assign a technician and operator to every active well.</li>\n<li>Order repairs before the technical condition of the well drops below 50%.</li>\n<li>Maintain a cash reserve of at least three times your daily operating costs.</li>\n<li>Buy transport with a capacity of about 120% of your production — leave a safety margin.</li>\n<li>Hire an HR Director as the first step in building the board — without him you cannot recruit the rest of the directors.</li>\n<li>Regularly check the Logistics panel — high transport losses are a signal to replace the route or pipeline.</li>\n<li>Watch the price of oil — when it drops below 70 PLN/bbl, consider limiting production.</li>\n<li>Before taking out a loan, check if the installment does not exceed 30% of your daily income.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>🔴 Avoid this</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Do not start a well without an operator — you incur operating costs without any revenue.</li>\n<li>Do not ignore breakdown alerts — minor faults quickly turn into disasters.</li>\n<li>Do not buy multiple wells at once if you do not have employees for each of them.</li>\n<li>Do not take out loans during an oil market price crisis.</li>\n<li>Do not leave a full storage without a solution — surplus oil is lost irretrievably.</li>\n<li>Do not abuse the black market — every transaction increases the risk indicator and the amount of the potential fine.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>💰 How to grow your company quickly?</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Start with 1–2 wells in a region with high deposit richness.</li>\n<li>When you achieve a stable income for 2 days, invest in another well.</li>\n<li>Reinvest 70% of the profit into development, keep 30% as a financial cushion.</li>\n<li>When you have 4 or more wells, start completing the board in the Boardroom.</li>\n<li>Track your return on investment (ROI) — if it exceeds 7 days, something needs adjusting.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>🆘 I got into trouble — what now?</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Stop all wells that bring losses (costs higher than revenue).</li>\n<li>Sell unnecessary assets — old wells or excess equipment.</li>\n<li>Pay off the most urgent loan installments to stop penalty interest from accumulating.</li>\n<li>Launch only 1–2 most profitable wells and gradually rebuild capital.</li>\n<li>Use the <strong>Rescue Panel</strong> if you see a restructuring banner — it is not the end of the game.</li>\n</ol>' WHERE `slug` = 'tips';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'How to start playing?', `content_en` = '<h1>🛢️ OilCorp &mdash; How to start? Guide for beginners</h1>\n<h2>Who are you?</h2>\n<p>You are the boss of an oil company. Your task is simple:&nbsp;<strong>drill wells, extract oil, sell it and make money.</strong>&nbsp;The more you earn, the bigger company you build!</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Step 1 &mdash; Check your wallet 💰</h2>\n<p>At the top of the screen you see a bar with four fields:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>CASH</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; how much money you have to start</li>\n<li><strong>STORAGE</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; extracted oil goes here (e.g. 0.00 / 10 000 bbl)</li>\n<li><strong>OIL PRICE</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; how much you will get for each barrel</li>\n<li><strong>STATUS</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; whether your company is operating properly</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>💡 Remember the oil price &mdash; when it is high, sell as much as possible!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>Step 2 &mdash; Build the Board FIRST THING TO DO 🏛️</h2>\n<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️&nbsp;<strong>This is mandatory.</strong>&nbsp;Without department directors nothing will start &mdash; you won\'t hire employees, you won\'t assign them to wells, nothing will work.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Go to the&nbsp;<strong>BOARDROOM</strong>&nbsp;page.</p>\n<p>You must hire department directors. Start with these two &mdash; they are the most important at the beginning:</p>\n<h3>HR Director</h3>\n<p>Responsible for recruiting employees.&nbsp;<strong>Without him you cannot hire anyone.</strong><br>Click the empty HR seat &rarr; Start recruitment &rarr; choose region &rarr; wait for the candidate to be ready &rarr; hire.</p>\n<h3>Technical Director</h3>\n<p>Responsible for the technical department.&nbsp;<strong>Without him, the wells won\'t operate smoothly.</strong><br>Same thing &mdash; click the Technical seat &rarr; recruit &rarr; hire.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>💡 Recruitment takes a while &mdash; start it and come back in a few minutes. Meanwhile, you can buy your first location on the map!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>Step 3 &mdash; Buy your first well 🗺️</h2>\n<p>Go to the&nbsp;<strong>MAP</strong>&nbsp;page (or click the \"Buy well\" button).</p>\n<p>On the globe you will see colored markers &mdash; these are available locations to buy. Each has:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: rgb(241, 196, 15);\"><strong>Purchase price</strong></span>&nbsp;&mdash; how much you will pay for the plot</li>\n<li><strong>Region richness</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; the higher it is, the more oil you will extract</li>\n<li><strong>Terrain type</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; onshore is cheaper to operate than offshore</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>💡 For a start, buy the&nbsp;<strong>cheapest onshore location</strong>&nbsp;with decent richness. Do not overpay &mdash; at the beginning every penny counts!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Click the location &rarr; confirm purchase &rarr; you have your first well! 🎉</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Step 4 &mdash; Hire technical employees 👷</h2>\n<p>Got the directors? Now it\'s time for employees for the well.</p>\n<p>Go to the&nbsp;<strong>TECHNICAL</strong>&nbsp;page &rarr;&nbsp;<strong>CANDIDATES</strong>&nbsp;tab.</p>\n<p>You need two people for each well:</p>\n<h3>Operator</h3>\n<p>Find a candidate with the&nbsp;<strong>Operator</strong>&nbsp;role and click \"Hire\".</p>\n<h3>Technician</h3>\n<p>Find a candidate with the&nbsp;<strong>Technician</strong>&nbsp;role (e.g. Maintenance Engineer) and click \"Hire\".</p>\n<p>Then go to the&nbsp;<strong>WELL PERSONNEL</strong>&nbsp;tab and assign both employees to your well.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>💡 Don\'t just look at the skill &mdash; also look at the salary! Skill 6 for 20,000/mo. is better than skill 8 for 80,000/mo. when you are just starting.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>Step 5 &mdash; Wait for oil ⏳</h2>\n<p>The game works in&nbsp;<strong>ticks</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; every few minutes the system calculates the production of all wells. After the first tick, your well will start filling the storage with oil.</p>\n<p>You can track progress in the&nbsp;<strong>PRODUCTION</strong>&nbsp;tab in the technical panel.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>💡 Green well status = producing. If you see anything else (e.g. \"No operator\"), go back to step 4!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>Step 6 &mdash; Sell the oil 📈</h2>\n<p>When you have oil in your storage, it\'s time to make a profit! Go to the&nbsp;<strong>OIL MARKET</strong>&nbsp;page.</p>\n<p>You can:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Post a sell offer</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; you set the price and wait for the market to settle it</li>\n<li><strong>Sell instantly</strong>&nbsp;at the current price</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>💡 Watch the oil price in the bar at the top. If it is e.g. $90 &mdash; sell immediately. If $50 &mdash; maybe it is worth waiting for a better price.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>Step 7 &mdash; Grow your company 🏗️</h2>\n<p>Got your first money? Time to grow!</p>\n<p><strong>What to do next (in order):</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Buy a second well</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; more wells = more oil = more money</li>\n<li><strong>Upgrade equipment</strong>&nbsp;on the well (Wells tab &rarr; Upgrade) &mdash; higher tier = better production</li>\n<li><strong>Complete the Board</strong>&nbsp;with the remaining directors (Finance, Legal, Logistics) &mdash; each gives bonuses</li>\n<li><strong>Take a loan from the bank</strong>&nbsp;if you want to develop faster &mdash; but pay the installments on time!</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>Step 8 &mdash; Keep an eye on your wells 🔧</h2>\n<p>Wells break down! From time to time, check the&nbsp;<strong>INCIDENTS</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>SAFETY</strong>&nbsp;tabs.</p>\n<p>If a well has a status other than \"Active\" &mdash; something is wrong:</p>\n<table style=\"width: 100%; height: 147.157px;\">\n<thead>\n<tr style=\"height: 10px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 24.5517%; height: 10px;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(241, 196, 15);\">Status</span></th>\n<th style=\"width: 37.5629%; height: 10px;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(241, 196, 15);\">What it means</span></th>\n<th style=\"width: 34.6107%; height: 10px;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(241, 196, 15);\">What to do</span></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 19.5938px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 24.5517%; height: 19.5938px;\">No operator</td>\n<td style=\"width: 37.5629%; height: 19.5938px;\">No operator assigned</td>\n<td style=\"width: 34.6107%; height: 19.5938px;\">Hire and assign an operator</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 19.5938px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 24.5517%; height: 19.5938px;\">No technician</td>\n<td style=\"width: 37.5629%; height: 19.5938px;\">No technician assigned</td>\n<td style=\"width: 34.6107%; height: 19.5938px;\">Hire and assign a technician</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 19.5938px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 24.5517%; height: 19.5938px;\">Suspended (cash)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 37.5629%; height: 19.5938px;\">No money for operating costs</td>\n<td style=\"width: 34.6107%; height: 19.5938px;\">Sell oil or take a loan</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 19.5938px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 24.5517%; height: 19.5938px;\">Suspended (storage)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 37.5629%; height: 19.5938px;\">Storage is full</td>\n<td style=\"width: 34.6107%; height: 19.5938px;\">Sell oil!</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 19.5938px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 24.5517%; height: 19.5938px;\">Broken</td>\n<td style=\"width: 37.5629%; height: 19.5938px;\">Zero technical condition, well stopped</td>\n<td style=\"width: 34.6107%; height: 19.5938px;\">Order repair in the Tasks tab</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 19.5938px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 24.5517%; height: 19.5938px;\">Seized by bailiff</td>\n<td style=\"width: 37.5629%; height: 19.5938px;\">Debts &mdash; bailiff took over the well</td>\n<td style=\"width: 34.6107%; height: 19.5938px;\">Pay off obligations in the Bank</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 19.5938px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 24.5517%; height: 19.5938px;\">Contaminated</td>\n<td style=\"width: 37.5629%; height: 19.5938px;\">Produces with a penalty after an incident</td>\n<td style=\"width: 34.6107%; height: 19.5938px;\">Wait or order cleanup</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr>\n<h2>What NOT to do at the beginning ❌</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>❌ Do not buy a well before you have at least the HR and Technical Directors &mdash; you won\'t be able to hire anyone anyway</li>\n<li>❌ Do not buy 5 wells at once &mdash; you won\'t have the people or cash for costs</li>\n<li>❌ Do not hire employees with salaries higher than you earn &mdash; you will go bankrupt</li>\n<li>❌ Do not ignore alerts &mdash; red messages are serious warnings</li>\n<li>❌ Do not enter the&nbsp;<strong>Black Market</strong>&nbsp;until you have a stable company &mdash; the penalties are painful!</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>Golden Rule 🏆</h2>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>First the Board, then the people, then the wells.</strong><br>One well-staffed well with a full team is better than three empty ones.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<p><em>Good luck, oil magnate!</em> 🛢️💰</p>' WHERE `slug` = 'nawigacja';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Boardroom', `content_en` = '<h2>Boardroom — build your team</h2>\n<p>The Boardroom is where you assemble your company\'s executive management. Each director gives the company tangible bonuses and unlocks game features.</p>\n<h3>How to start?</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to the <strong>Boardroom</strong> tab.</li>\n<li>On the board you can see 9 empty seats (+ You as the CEO).</li>\n<li>Click an empty seat → the recruitment panel will appear.</li>\n<li><strong>First person to hire: HR Director</strong> — without him you cannot recruit the rest of the board.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Recruitment process</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Select the search region (PL, UK, US, NO, PH, AE...) — affects the candidate profile.</li>\n<li>Select the search time (1h / 2h / 4h) — longer = better candidates.</li>\n<li>Wait for the results — 2–3 candidates will appear to choose from.</li>\n<li>Evaluate the candidates by skills and expected salary, click <strong>Hire</strong>.</li>\n<li>Candidates expire after some time — do not delay!</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Board roles</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>👥 HR Director</strong> — recruits other directors. <em>Required first.</em></li>\n<li><strong>🔧 Technical Director</strong> — bonuses to well maintenance, unlocks advanced repairs.</li>\n<li><strong>💰 Financial Director</strong> — better credit terms, oversight of cash flow.</li>\n<li><strong>⚖️ Legal Director</strong> — regulatory compliance, protection against fines.</li>\n<li><strong>🚛 Logistics Director</strong> — transport optimization, lower pipeline losses. Panel accessible by clicking his business card.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Firing a director</h3>\n<p>Click the employee → <strong>Fire</strong>. Dismissal is immediate. Note: if you fire the HR Director, you cannot recruit new directors until you hire a new one.</p>\n<h3>Skill and seniority</h3>\n<p>Each director has a rating in 5 skills (organization, negotiations, analytics, strategy, ethics). Higher average score = stronger bonus for the company. Seniority grows over time of employment.</p>' WHERE `slug` = 'boardroom';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Black Market for Oil', `content_en` = '<h2>Black Market — high profits, high risk</h2>\n<p>The black market allows you to sell oil outside the official market at prices 130–200% of market value. But every transaction carries the risk of detection and a financial penalty.</p>\n<h3>How does it work?</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Offers on the black market appear automatically every few ticks.</li>\n<li>Each offer has: the number of barrels, price per bbl and the % risk of detection.</li>\n<li>By accepting the offer, you lose oil from storage and receive cash.</li>\n<li>If you are detected — you pay a fine and your credit score drops.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Black Score — risk indicator</h3>\n<p>Every transaction on the black market increases your <strong>Black Score</strong> (0–100). The higher the score, the greater the chance of detection on the next transaction.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>0–30</strong> — low risk, penalty ~7–15% of cash upon getting caught.</li>\n<li><strong>30–60</strong> — medium risk, penalty ~10–20%.</li>\n<li><strong>60–100</strong> — high risk, penalty up to 30%+ cash.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Black Score <strong>drops automatically</strong> every tick when you are not trading on the black market. Wait a few ticks between transactions.</p>\n<h3>Detection risk</h3>\n<p>Effective risk = base risk of the offer + (Black Score × 0.5%). E.g. an offer with a 20% base risk at a Black Score of 40 gives a 40% chance of detection.</p>\n<h3>Penalty for detection</h3>\n<p>When you get caught:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The oil is sold anyway (revenue is kept).</li>\n<li>The penalty is deducted from the account — proportional to the Black Score and your balance.</li>\n<li>Credit Score drops by a few points.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the black market occasionally, not as a main source of income.</li>\n<li>Watch the Black Score — when it exceeds 50, wait a few ticks.</li>\n<li>Choose offers with a low % base risk.</li>\n<li>Do not trade during a financial crisis — a penalty could finish you off.</li>\n</ul>' WHERE `slug` = 'czarny-rynek';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Logistics Department', `content_en` = '<h2>Logistics Department — control oil transport</h2>\n<p>The Logistics Panel gives a full picture of how oil travels from the well to the market — how much is lost in transport, how much it costs, and where the weak points are.</p>\n\n<h3>🏭 Logistics hubs — the foundation of transport</h3>\n<p>Before oil hits the market, it must go through a <strong>logistics hub</strong> — a transfer station managed by the system. Your wells are assigned to them automatically or manually by the Logistics Director. A hub has a specific capacity (slots) and technical condition — when its condition drops, losses increase. A detailed description of hubs can be found in the <strong>Logistics hubs</strong> section in this help department.</p>\n\n<h3>How to open the panel?</h3>\n<p>Go to the <strong>Boardroom</strong> tab, click the <strong>Logistics Director\'s</strong> business card, and then <strong>Open Logistics Panel</strong>.</p>\n\n<h3>What can be seen in the panel?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Total production</strong> — how many barrels were produced in the current cycle.</li>\n<li><strong>Delivered to market</strong> — how many barrels actually reached the sale.</li>\n<li><strong>Transport losses</strong> — how much oil was lost (leaks, evaporation, hub breakdowns).</li>\n<li><strong>Transport efficiency [%]</strong> — the ratio of delivered to produced. The goal is above 92%.</li>\n<li><strong>Transport operational costs</strong> — total cost of all transport per cycle.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Breakdown of transport types</h3>\n<p>The panel shows what transport your wells use and what their losses are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Pipeline</strong> — the lowest losses (2–5%). High one-time installation cost, low running costs.</li>\n<li><strong>Trucks</strong> — higher losses (5–12%). Cheap and easy to start, but expensive in the long run.</li>\n<li><strong>Tanker</strong> — intermediate losses. Profitable with high production from offshore wells.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Alert messages</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>🔴 No active wells</strong> — no well is producing; there is nothing to transport.</li>\n<li><strong>🔴 Losses above 15%</strong> — critical losses. Immediately check the condition of hubs and pipelines.</li>\n<li><strong>🟡 Losses above 8%</strong> — elevated losses. Recommended inspection of transport infrastructure and hub condition.</li>\n<li><strong>🟡 Efficiency below 85%</strong> — something is losing oil on the way. Check if hubs are in Eco mode or have high condition.</li>\n<li><strong>🟢 Transport operates optimally</strong> — everything is functional, no need for intervention.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>How to improve efficiency?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Check hub condition — a hub below 50% condition significantly increases losses. Repair it.</li>\n<li>Replace truck transport with a pipeline — the higher installation cost quickly pays off due to lower losses.</li>\n<li>Regularly repair pipelines — damaged ones have a several times higher percentage of losses.</li>\n<li>Make sure that each well has transport adapted to its scale of production.</li>\n</ul>' WHERE `slug` = 'logistyka';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Selling a well', `content_en` = '<h2>Selling a well — when and how?</h2>\n<p>You can sell a well when it is unprofitable, damaged, or you want to free up capital for better investments. The sale is irreversible.</p>\n<h3>How to sell?</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to the <strong>Technical</strong> tab.</li>\n<li>Click the well → <strong>Sale</strong> tab.</li>\n<li>The system will calculate the estimated price.</li>\n<li>Confirm the sale — funds arrive in your account immediately.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>What affects the sale price?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Daily well profit</strong> — the main component of the valuation. The higher the EBITDA, the higher the price.</li>\n<li><strong>Technical condition</strong> — a broken well is worth less.</li>\n<li><strong>Equipment tier</strong> — wells with better equipment have a higher residual value.</li>\n<li><strong>Geological layer</strong> — deeper deposits are valued higher.</li>\n<li><strong>Wear level</strong> — high wear lowers the valuation.</li>\n<li><strong>Black market equipment</strong> — lowers the valuation by an additional multiplier.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Sale cooldown</h3>\n<p>After purchasing a well, there is a cooldown period during which it cannot be sold. This prevents trading in wells instead of exploiting them.</p>\n<h3>When is it worth selling?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>The well has been making losses for a long time (OPEX &gt; revenue) and there is no chance of improvement.</li>\n<li>The deposit is almost exhausted — production drops to minimal levels.</li>\n<li>You need capital to buy a better location.</li>\n<li>The bailiff enters and you prefer to sell than lose it for free.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>After the sale</h3>\n<p>Employees assigned to the sold well become free and you can assign them to other wells. Storage and transport are not sold together with the well.</p>' WHERE `slug` = 'sprzedaz';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Map — buying wells', `content_en` = '<h2>Map — how to buy a well?</h2>\n<p>The world map is where you buy new locations and decide where to drill. It is one of the most important investment decisions.</p>\n<h3>How to buy a well?</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to the <strong>Map</strong> tab.</li>\n<li>Browse available locations — click a pin on the map or a row in the list.</li>\n<li>Check the location parameters (deposit richness, geological layer, region, purchase price).</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Buy well</strong> — funds are deducted immediately.</li>\n<li>The well appears on the dashboard in idle status — assign an operator and technician to start production.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Location parameters</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Oil Richness</strong> — deposit richness (1–100). Affects the base production of barrels/tick. Higher = more oil.</li>\n<li><strong>Geological layer</strong>:\n  <ul>\n  <li>🟡 <strong>Shallow</strong> — cheap drilling, little oil, low risk.</li>\n  <li>🟠 <strong>Mid-depth</strong> — good balance of cost to production.</li>\n  <li>🔴 <strong>Deep</strong> — expensive, but high production.</li>\n  <li>⚫ <strong>Ultra Deep</strong> — very expensive, maximum production, high risk of blowout.</li>\n  </ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Regional risk</strong> — affects the frequency of disasters and political incidents.</li>\n<li><strong>Purchase price</strong> — one-time cost of acquiring the location.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>What to look for?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Compare the purchase price with the projected daily revenue — is the ROI acceptable?</li>\n<li>Wells in stable regions have fewer breakdowns — choose PL or UK to start.</li>\n<li>Do not buy a well if you do not have cash for OPEX for at least 3 days.</li>\n<li>Always have an employee ready to assign before you buy another well.</li>\n</ul>' WHERE `slug` = 'mapa';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Employees', `content_en` = '<h2>Employees — the key to smooth company operations</h2>\n<p>An oil company needs two types of employees: <strong>technical staff</strong> operates the wells, and the <strong>board</strong> provides strategic bonuses and unlocks advanced features.</p>\n\n<h3>Technical staff (HR)</h3>\n<p>Manage them in the <strong>HR</strong> tab.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>👨‍💼 Operator</strong> — manages the daily operation of the well. Without an operator, the well does not produce oil. Skill rating (1–10) directly multiplies production efficiency.</li>\n<li><strong>🔧 Technician</strong> — keeps equipment in working order. Without a technician, the technical condition drops twice as fast. High skill level significantly slows down equipment wear.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Employee specializations</h3>\n<p>Some employees have an additional specialization that gives a tangible bonus:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>HSE Inspector / Safety Engineer</strong> — reduces the risk of blowouts and major disasters.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance Engineer</strong> — slower equipment wear, lower repair costs.</li>\n<li><strong>Production Engineer</strong> — increases oil extraction efficiency.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Company Board (Boardroom)</h3>\n<p>Manage your executive staff in the <strong>Boardroom</strong> tab. Recruitment is done through the HR Director.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>👥 HR Director</strong> — allows the recruitment of other board members. Hire him first.</li>\n<li><strong>🔧 Technical Director</strong> — unlocks advanced options in the Technical tab.</li>\n<li><strong>💰 Financial Director</strong> — improves credit terms and company credit rating.</li>\n<li><strong>⚖️ Legal Director</strong> — handles regulatory affairs and contracts.</li>\n<li><strong>🚛 Logistics Director</strong> — manages oil transport and optimizes transport costs. Panel accessible by clicking his business card in the Boardroom.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>How to recruit for the board?</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to the <strong>Boardroom</strong> tab and click an empty seat on the board.</li>\n<li>Choose the search region and recruitment time (1 h / 2 h / 4 h) — longer time means better candidates.</li>\n<li>After the time elapses, candidates will appear to choose from — evaluate their skills and expected salary.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Hire</strong>. Remember: candidates have a limited validity time.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>How to hire technicians and operators?</h3>\n<p>Go to the <strong>HR</strong> tab. Candidates appear randomly. Check their skill level and specialization — a good employee means tangibly higher revenue and lower repair costs.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"color: #c8a84b; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(200,168,75,0.25); padding-bottom: 8px;\">Staff Training and Traits 🎓</h3>\n<p class=\"help-p\">Your technical staff are not nameless machines. They have their own unique traits, such as <strong>Loyalty, Corruption Risk or Ambition</strong>. These traits directly affect their performance and demands.</p>\n<p class=\"help-p\">To improve the skills and morale of the crew, send them to <strong>Trainings</strong> available in the HR tab. A trained employee works faster and unlocks new bonuses.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"color: #c8a84b; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(200,168,75,0.25); padding-bottom: 8px;\">Strikes and Raise Demands 📢</h3>\n<p class=\"help-p\">When crew morale drops or they think they earn too little, they can issue a <strong>Raise Demand</strong>.</p>\n<ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n    <li class=\"help-p\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>Your options:</strong> You can accept the full amount, send a smaller counteroffer (a <em>Wage Negotiator</em> employee helps a lot with this), reject the request, or postpone it.</li>\n    <li class=\"help-p\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>Strike:</strong> Too many rejected requests and low morale will lead to escalation and a strike. You will be forced to sit down to multi-round negotiations. Your chances of a cheap settlement depend on the skills of the assigned HR Board!</li>\n</ul>' WHERE `slug` = 'pracownicy';

UPDATE `game_help_pages` SET `title_en` = 'Logistics hubs', `content_en` = '<h2>Logistics hubs — what is it and why do I need it?</h2>\n<p>Imagine a hub as a <strong>transfer station</strong> — a warehouse with a ramp, through which oil from your wells reaches the market. Without a hub, oil \"gets stuck\" in the field and will not reach the sale. The better the hub, the more wells you can connect to it and the less oil is lost in transport.</p>\n\n<h3>🏗️ Types of hubs — which one to choose?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>🔹 Small (local)</strong> — serves a few wells in one area. Cheap to maintain, but quickly clogs up when production grows. Good for a start or for wells in difficult terrain.</li>\n<li><strong>🔷 Medium (regional)</strong> — serves a dozen or so wells in the entire region. The golden mean: good capacity, reasonable costs. Enough for most players for most of the game.</li>\n<li><strong>🔶 Large (continental)</strong> — serves dozens of wells across the continent. Necessary when you build an oil empire with wells in different countries. High cost, but capacity is no limitation.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>⚙️ Work modes — how does a hub work?</h3>\n<p>Every hub has a work mode switch. It works like a gear in a car:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>🟢 Eco — fewer losses, slower</strong> — the hub works calmly, wears out slowly and oil losses are minimal. Choose when oil is expensive, the hub is in poor technical condition or you want to save it before a technician arrives.</li>\n<li><strong>🔵 Standard — normal traffic</strong> — default mode. A balance between speed and wear. In 90% of cases, you will stick with this mode.</li>\n<li><strong>🔴 Turbo — fast, but wears the hub</strong> — the hub pushes through the maximum amount of oil in a given cycle. Useful when you have a lot of oil to push and a full storage — but the hub loses condition faster. Do not use for long without repair.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>📊 What do the numbers on the hub card mean?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Condition (e.g. 87.5%)</strong> — the technical condition of the hub. Decreases over time and depends on the work mode. When it drops below 30% — oil losses increase dramatically. Click \"Repair\" to restore to 100%.</li>\n<li><strong>Wear</strong> — the rate at which the hub degrades every cycle. Turbo mode doubles this rate.</li>\n<li><strong>Slots (e.g. 3/6)</strong> — how many wells are currently connected to the hub out of available places. When all slots are taken — you cannot assign a new well without disconnecting another.</li>\n<li><strong>Level</strong> — the internal level of the hub. Higher level = greater capacity and lower base losses.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>🔴 Hub statuses — what is happening?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>✅ Active</strong> — the hub works normally. Oil flows through it every cycle.</li>\n<li><strong>⏸ Suspended</strong> — the hub is stopped manually by the admin. No oil will flow. Wells connected to a suspended hub lose transport efficiency.</li>\n<li><strong>🔧 Broken</strong> — the hub suffered a breakdown. Production through it is limited or suspended. Repair required.</li>\n<li><strong>🚫 Disabled</strong> — the hub is permanently disabled from the system. It does not serve any wells.</li>\n<li><strong>🏗️ Under construction</strong> — the hub is currently starting up. It does not handle transport yet.</li>\n<li><strong>⚠️ Overloaded</strong> — more oil flows through the hub than it can handle. Some oil is lost. Connect fewer wells or switch to Turbo mode.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>💡 Practical tips</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Check hub condition regularly — repair before it drops below 50%.</li>\n<li>Do not fill the hub to the last slot — leave 1–2 empty places as a buffer.</li>\n<li>Turbo mode is a last resort — use it short-term during large production backlogs.</li>\n<li>When a hub is overloaded, check the slots first — maybe disconnecting an unprofitable well is enough.</li>\n<li>A large hub in poor condition gives worse results than a small hub in good condition.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"color: #c8a84b; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(200,168,75,0.25); padding-bottom: 8px;\">Managing Hub Work Modes ⚙️</h3>\n<p class=\"help-p\">Hub owners and their main tenants can manage the work mode of their logistics node at any time, adapting it to the current budget situation.</p>\n<ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; list-style-type: square; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n    <li class=\"help-p\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>Eco:</strong> The Hub works slower and provides lower transport throughput, but its maintenance costs drop drastically. Ideal for times of crisis.</li>\n    <li class=\"help-p\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>Standard:</strong> Balanced maintenance.</li>\n    <li class=\"help-p\" style=\"margin-bottom: 8px;\"><strong>Turbo:</strong> Significantly increases the maximum throughput of pipelines connected to the Hub, but generates massive maintenance costs.</li>\n</ul>' WHERE `slug` = 'huby';
